\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri7467\sl244\slmult1\sb236\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 This powerful feature lets you shim (change or adjust) the Front and/or Rear Frame Mounts for the upper control arms (A Arms or Wishbones).\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You can shim this arm and have all other suspension\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 measurements\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 change\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 just\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 as if you had made the change on the\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 actual car.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri7483\sl244\slmult1\sb229\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 For example, at the Main Screen you\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 can change the Frame Mounts for the upper arms and only that measurement changes.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 That is a useful method when you are first entering measurements for the car.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 However, on the actual car, if you, say, shim out the front, left Frame Pivot, you will likely move the upper ball joint out and back, changing\expnd8\expndtw40\charscalex100  \expnd0\expndtw0 camber\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 caster.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 could\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 also\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 push the left tire down somewhat, tilting up the left side of the chassis.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 All measurements tilt up, and there would be some small change in some measurements moving to the right. This feature can simulate all these changes\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\sl-221\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 that\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 you\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 would\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 see\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 on\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 actual\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 car.\expnd9\expndtw45  \expnd0\expndtw0 See\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 Figure\expnd0\expndtw-2  2.29.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb8\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri365\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 To use this feature, first pick whether you will Add or Remove shims for either the Front or Back mount, or both. Then select whether you want to use standard sixteenth\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 (1/16) and eighth (1/8) inch shims, or to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 enter some\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 other 'Custom'\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 shim\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 adjustment. After your selection, the lower inputs will become enabled as appropriate.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Selecting 'No Shims' disables the lower inputs and keeps that mounting point unchanged.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The total shim thickness will be displayed for both the Front and Back mount, and the change in Caster and Camber.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery725\footery743\margtsxn1100\margbsxn940\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb9\f0\fs15\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li224\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20
