\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb222\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri401\sl244\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 To save a Suspension File, you will be presented with the Save\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 screen as shown above.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The program\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 suggests a new suspension name which is the same as the current suspension name shown at the top of the Main Screen.\expnd12\expndtw59  \expnd0\expndtw0 If you want to save your changes to the same name, simply click on OK.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This will update the current suspension file with your latest changes.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri358\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 If you want to save the current set of suspension specs with your changes to a new name\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 (and leave the current suspension file\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 in the Library unchanged), then click on the suggested file name and modify it as you want.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 For example, in the window shown above, you may want to add 2 to the current name CAMBERTEST to create CAMBERTEST2 to indicate this is the 2nd\expnd16\expndtw80\charscalex100  \expnd0\expndtw0 revision of CAMBERTEST.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This is the safest way\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to make changes, because you can always\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 return\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 to an earlier version and see what you had done.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri422\sl244\slmult1\tx8177\tx9901\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Because the Suspension Analyzer is a 32 bit program (not compatible with the older Windows 3.1), it can use most any type of file name.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The names can be up to 50 characters long and can include spaces, and upper case and lower case letters.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 However, there are certain limitations for file names, as they can \f8\b1\i1 not \f0\b0\i0 contain certain characters, like\tab /\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 \'5C\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 :\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 |\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 >\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 <\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 *\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 ?\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 \'93\tab .\expnd6\expndtw28  \expnd0\expndtw0 The\expnd-2\expndtw-11  \expnd0\expndtw0 program will warn you if you use an illegal character.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb7\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Suspension files are saved to folders (directories) you have created in the 3D-DATA folder (directory) in\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 SUPSANZR\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 folder (directory) under PERFTRNS.PTI folder (directory).\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You \f8\b1\i1 can \f0\b0\i0 copy Suspension Analyzer files from programs on other\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery725\footery744\margtsxn1100\margbsxn940\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li359\ri917\sl244\slmult1\sb113\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 computers to this folder (directory) and they will be found by the program.\expnd16\expndtw80  \expnd0\expndtw0 The Suspension Analyzer \f8\b1\i1 will \f0\b0\i0 read files produced with Performance Trends\'92 Roll Center Calculator and Circle Track Analyzer, and BTS Software\'92s Double Wishbone Suspension Analysis Software (tm).\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Just copy\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 them\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 into a folder under the 3D-DATA folder (other than the Examples folder). The Save to Floppy and Open From Floppy commands discussed on page 29 are an alternate, perhaps easier way to copy files from one computer to another.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb9\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s10\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\sl240\slmult1\f2\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Advance\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 Open\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 or\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 Save\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw-2 Screen\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f2\fs28\b0\i0\par
