\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri7106\sl244\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 For the right side idler arm, you can also clearly see the top and bottom of the idler arm shaft.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The problem comes from measuring\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 these\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 points\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 accurately\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 enough\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 to determine\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 idler\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 arm\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 axis.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 Figure\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 4.4 If you assume you can only measure points accurate to 0.1 inch, then you need a large distance between the ends of the shaft to accurately determine the angle of the axis. See Figure 4.5.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This is a case where it is much more accurate to use the alternate measurement method described in Section\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri7056\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 2.8.5.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This method involves measuring the angles\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 idler\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 arm\expnd-1\expndtw-6  \expnd0\expndtw0 (or\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 steering\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 box)\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 shaft and length and angle of the idler arm or Pitman Arm.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 These angle and length measurements are all made referenced from the end of the arm that attaches to the center link.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This also makes it easy to make these measurements\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 at most any\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 time in\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the future, even after the car has been moved.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You can print the Steering Swivel Axis screen of Figure 4.6 when it is blank and use it as a separate worksheet.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery725\footery744\margtsxn1100\margbsxn940\pard\plain\s11\ls23\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\fi-1\ri811\sl244\slmult1\sb111\tx360\tx625\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Be\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 sure to mark the center of the tire patch at both the front\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 and back of each tire.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This is not for toe in determination, but for identifying the exact tire track from left to right.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See Figure 4.7.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb3\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s11\ls23\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri1057\sl244\slmult1\tx626\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Make the other measurements required like Camber and Toe In.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You can also record other\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 info like Tread Width and Tire \expnd0\expndtw-2 Circumference.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb3\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s11\ls23\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri1040\sl244\slmult1\tx626\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 At the bottom\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 of the Worksheet are several Other Specs you can\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 measure or estimate.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Several of these we already\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 set, like Steering type, Springs type, Roll\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Bar type before we printed the worksheet.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The Height of CG and % Front Braking are very difficult to measure or determine accurately.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Luckily they are only used for the % Anti-Dive calculation.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 It is recommended you estimate a Height of CG of 20\'94 and % Front Braking of 65% as typical for most cars.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb3\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s11\ls23\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri1316\sl244\slmult1\tx627\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 When \f8\b1\i1 all\expnd0\expndtw-1  \f0\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 measurements are done, roll the car off the drywall.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Draw\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 a line from\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the left and right wheel spindle centers marked in step 2.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This will be the \f8\b1\i1 axle \f0\b0\i0 line.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb4\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s11\ls23\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li625\fi-266\sl240\slmult1\tx625\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Draw\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 line\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 from\expnd-1\expndtw-5  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 front\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 back\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 tire\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 patch\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 dots.\expnd9\expndtw44  \expnd0\expndtw0 Where\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 this\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 line\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 crosses\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 axle\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 line\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 is\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 center\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 tire\expnd0\expndtw-2  patch.\par
