t1\sb1\f3\fs32\b1\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100 Static \expnd0\expndtw0 Analysis at Main\expnd-5\expndtw-23  \expnd0\expndtw0 Screen\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri8829\sl244\slmult1\sb239\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Back at the Main Screen, there are several useful calculations\expnd-3\expndtw-13  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd-2\expndtw-12  \expnd0\expndtw0 analyze this suspension.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri434\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Figure 4.16.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Calculations like Roll Center Left/Right and Height, Caster, Anti-Dive %, etc. are calculated and shown in the Suspension Data table in the Output rows.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You may\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 have to click and slide the slide bar down to be able to see various sections of the Suspension Data table.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 If you click on the No View tab at the top (next to Front View, Side View, Top View tabs), you can display more of the table by eliminating the Suspension Layout drawing.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You can also click on File, then Print to print the entire table with all input and calculated output rows.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri434\sl244\slmult1\sb228\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The Suspension Layout drawing also shows several \'93gain\'94 calculations.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Gain means increase in a calculated number for a standard\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 amount\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 suspension\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 movement.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 standard\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 amount\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 suspension\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 movement\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 is\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 set\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 1\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 inch\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 dive\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 when\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 first get the program, and is identified at the top of the Layout Drawing.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This standard suspension movement for calculating gains can be changed in the Preferences menu.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See Section 2.2.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri365\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 For\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 example,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Left\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Camber\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Gain\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 shown\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 in\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Figure\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 4.16\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 -1.27\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 degrees\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 means\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 left\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 camber\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 decreases\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 (goes\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 more\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 negative) by 1.27 degrees with 1 inch of dive.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Negative Camber Gain is desirable in a race car suspension, so the tire camber goes more negative in corners, during dive and roll.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See Appendix 2.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery725\footery744\margtsxn1100\marg